ime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013ivEDhZSzBU689j1PgMYA6", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377108, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013ivEDhZSzBU689j1PgMYA6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380894, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **The fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212, but the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the function's own description. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B5syMUcXTsxpb6xMPbGnpL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012xrrxiC3qweRx5qAX9ULkw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012wrCXa6e7M9LPVC68qg5KU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Asprt