ll}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **The fix:** I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212, but the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the function's own description. I haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}